# Whitelist-only: ignore everything except *.md, *.py, *.vac, *.json, *.cs, *.cslist,
# *.txt, and *.jpg only under Saves/scene/ (any subfolder depth).
# Under Custom/, only Custom/Scripts/ may contain trackable files; other Custom/
# subtrees stay ignored while extension rules apply elsewhere as before.
# (`*` ignores; `!*/` lets Git traverse directories so `!` rules can match.)
*
!*/
!.gitignore
!**/*.md
!**/*.py
!/Saves/
!/Saves/scene/
!Saves/scene/**/*.jpg
!**/*.vac
!**/*.json
!**/*.cs
!**/*.cslist
!**/*.txt

# Custom/: only Scripts/ is eligible for the extensions above; rest of Custom stays ignored.
Custom/**
!Custom/Scripts/
!Custom/Scripts/**

# After whitelist: hide paths whose components contain these substrings (case variants).
# Later rules win; * does not cross '/' so each path segment is checked.
*pose*
*Pose*
*appearance*
*Appearance*
